---
import StandardLifecycleNotice from "../../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import StandardPageLayout from "../../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../../data/standards/hgb/drs02.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  subtitle={metadata.nativeTitle}
  framework="hgb"
  status={metadata.status}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Part of the DRS consolidation wave" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Why withdrawn" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Status summary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <StandardLifecycleNotice
    type="withdrawn"
    explanation="This standard has been withdrawn."
    targetStatus="Replaced by DRS 21"
    link="/germany/drs/drs21"
    linkText="View DRS 21"
  />

  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Part of the DRS consolidation wave</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card warn">
<div class="ctitle">Part of the DRS consolidation wave</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 2 was the DRSC's original, general cash flow statement standard, elaborating the Kapitalflussrechnung requirement established under §297(1) HGB (covered in the earlier HGB poster series). Reflecting how differently a bank's or insurer's own cash flows are structured compared to an ordinary trading/manufacturing enterprise, the DRSC ALSO issued two dedicated sector-specific companion standards: DRS 2-10 for credit institutions, and DRS 2-20 for insurance undertakings – a genuinely distinctive three-standard cluster covering the same underlying statement across different industries.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Why withdrawn – replaced by a single, unified successor</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card info">
<div class="ctitle">Why withdrawn – replaced by a single, unified successor</div>
<div class="principle">The BMJ formally withdrew DRS 2 (and its two sector companions) on 8 April 2014, with the Bundesanzeiger announcement of the new DRS 21 "Kapitalflussrechnung" – a single, UNIFIED cash flow statement standard that folded the general rules AND the credit-institution/insurance-specific adaptations into ONE document (using dedicated internal annexes for the sector-specific content, rather than entirely separate standalone standards). Last applicable to fiscal years beginning on or before 31 December 2014.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Status summary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card">
<div class="ctitle">Status summary</div>
<div class="td-table">
<div class="th"><span>Field</span><span>Detail</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Original topic</span><span>Cash flow statement – general (DRS 2), credit institutions (2-10), insurers (2-20)</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Withdrawn</span><span>8 April 2014</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Successor</span><span><strong>DRS 21 – Kapitalflussrechnung</strong> (unified standard with sector-specific annexes)</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Last applicable</span><span>Fiscal years beginning on or before 31.12.2014</span></div>
</div>
</div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
